  "id": "COMPOUND:10898 - PROTEIN:6154",
  "verbalization": "Tucaresol appears to interact with Prelamin-A/C through a series of molecular pathways, with the drug targeting multiple enzymes in the SDR family, including Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9. These enzymes are subsequently targeted by compounds like Ajugaciliatin E and N-Methyltyramine, which in turn affect Prelamin-A/C. The evidence suggests a potential indirect relationship between Tucaresol and Prelamin-A/C, mediated through these intermediate targets. The observed scores indicate a moderate level of confidence in this pathway, though the exact mechanism of action remains unclear. The integration of these targets highlights the complexity of the interaction network, emphasizing the role of enzyme-mediated pathways in modulating the effects of Tucaresol on cellular processes.",
